shape theory.physics.time : theory.physics.lattice, theory.transformation-law, theory.discreteness {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 2.5 (Time).
// Time is the transformation law evaluating, not another spatial
// direction.
//
// Every shape transforms: M' = f(C, S). That evaluation IS a
// moment. The transition from M to M' is a "tick."
//
// Shape A's context includes its neighbors (via contact), so A's
// next moment depends on B's current moment and vice versa. This
// mutual dependence forces simultaneous evaluation across the
// entire connected lattice, producing a collective tick.
//
// Once M' = f(C, S) evaluates, the prior character is gone.
// Multiple prior configurations can map to the same current
// configuration (many-to-one), so reconstruction is not generally
// possible. This is the arrow of time: not statistical tendency
// but structural fact about evaluation.
//
// Space is how the lattice IS. Time is how the lattice CHANGES.
// Result: n+1 spacetime (n spatial + 1 temporal).
//
// Derives from: theory.physics.lattice,
//               theory.transformation-law, theory.discreteness
  """
}
